# Gateway pipeline

Register request middleware in dependency order. Run routing before policies that depend on endpoint metadata. Authenticate the caller before evaluating authorization. Then map the endpoints used by the gateway.

For an ASP.NET Core gateway using YARP and a named authorization policy:

```csharp
app.UseRouting();
app.UseAuthentication();
app.UseAuthorization();
app.MapReverseProxy().RequireAuthorization("GatewayAccess");
```

Register the proxy, authentication scheme and policy during startup. Add GraphQL or WebSocket support when the gateway exposes those protocols.
